$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"Git"$$FG$

A read-only git client.  It fetches a repository's packfile, resolves deltas and writes the working tree of the default branch to disk.  There is no .git directory and no loose objects -- the OS has no DEFLATE encoder, so nothing can be committed or pushed back.

$FG,5$--- Load it ---$FG$

The network stack must be up first ($LK,"Net Start",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Start.ZC"$ -- an IP should show in the Network Report).  Then:

$ID,2$$FG,2$#include "C:/Home/Net/Programs/SSH/SSH"$FG$   only needed for ssh urls
$FG,2$#include "C:/Home/Net/Programs/Git/Git"$FG$$ID,-2$

Load SSH $UL,1$before$UL,0$ git.  Git.ZC pulls in the ssh transport only if the SSH client is already there; HTTPS-only use needs just the second line.

$FG,5$--- Clone ---$FG$

All three url shapes real git accepts work:

$ID,2$$FG,2$GitClone("https://github.com/octocat/Hello-World");$FG$
$FG,2$GitClone("git@github.com:octocat/Hello-World.git");$FG$
$FG,2$GitClone("ssh://git@my.host:2222/srv/project.git");$FG$$ID,-2$

The clone lands in <current directory>/<repo name>, so $FG,2$Cd("::/Home");$FG$ first to pick where it goes.

A second argument renames the destination.  A bare name is created under the current directory; anything holding "/" or ":" is taken as a path:

$ID,2$$FG,2$GitClone("git@github.com:octocat/Hello-World.git", "Hello");$FG$
$FG,2$GitClone("https://host/user/repo", "::/Home/MyRepo");$FG$$ID,-2$

If the target directory already exists you get a No/Yes prompt before anything is written.  Each file prints as it lands, and big packs print progress while inflating and resolving deltas.  $FG,4$Esc$FG$ cancels during unpack and checkout; the network fetch itself is not cancellable.

$FG,5$--- SSH urls ---$FG$

git@host:path authenticates with the key in the agent, the same way real git does.  Generate a key once and install it on the server -- see $LK,"SSH",A="FI:::/Doc/SSH.DD"$.  After a reboot the key file is still on disk but the agent is empty, so:

$ID,2$$FG,2$SSHKeyLoad;$FG$
$FG,2$GitClone("git@github.com:username/repository.git");$FG$$ID,-2$

The login name comes from the url and defaults to "git".  The port defaults to 22 and can only be given in the ssh:// form, as in real git.

$FG,4$No host-key checking.$FG$  An active man-in-the-middle is not detected.

For a password login instead of a key, call the ssh path with explicit fields:

$ID,2$$FG,2$GitCloneSSH("192.168.1.10", 22, "root", "/srv/repo.git", NULL, "PASSWORD");$FG$$ID,-2$

$FG,5$--- List refs ---$FG$

The cheapest way to check a remote is reachable.  HTTPS only:

$ID,2$$FG,2$GitLsRemote("https://github.com/octocat/Hello-World");$FG$$ID,-2$

Prints every ref as sha + name, then a count.

$FG,5$--- Command reference ---$FG$

$ID,2$GitClone(url, dir=NULL)                       Clone the default branch's tree.  url may be https, git@host:path or ssh://.
GitLsRemote(url)                              List a remote's refs over HTTPS.
GitCloneSSH(host, port, user, repo, dir, pw)  Clone over SSH with explicit fields; pw only for password auth.
GitFetchToFile(url, path)                     Fetch the raw packfile and save it, nothing else.
SHA1Test                                      SHA-1 self-test.$ID,-2$

$FG,5$--- Limits ---$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,2$Read-only.$FG$  No commit, no push, no branch switching, no history: one checkout.

$FG,2$Default branch only.$FG$  HEAD is used if the server advertises it, else refs/heads/main or refs/heads/master, else the first ref.

$FG,2$Submodules$FG$ are skipped -- a gitlink entry carries no content in the pack.

$FG,2$Existing files$FG$ in the target are overwritten.

$FG,2$Big repos$FG$ are slow: delta resolution scans the object table per object.

$FG,2$GitHub over HTTPS$FG$ sometimes gates on a git/ User-Agent.  ssh is the reliable route.$ID,-2$

$FG,5$--- Source ---$FG$

$ID,2$$LK,"Git.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Git/Git.ZC"$        loader
$LK,"GitProto.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Git/GitProto.ZC"$   url parsing, pkt-lines, ref discovery, pack fetch
$LK,"GitPack.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Git/GitPack.ZC"$    inflate, delta resolution, checkout, GitClone
$LK,"GitSSH.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Git/GitSSH.ZC"$     the pack protocol over an SSH exec channel
$LK,"GitSHA1.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Git/GitSHA1.ZC"$    SHA-1$ID,-2$

Deeper notes: $LK,"the git client guide",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Git/GitGuide.DD"$.
